title: '''example-data/'', the model setup points to, names a friend''s skgrepo that is not there, and its README speaks of a ''lens'' no page for users defines.'
pid: 2bcbe483-ac15-4a57-9b69-8bd70495b4ff
body: |2-
  Its config lists Fred's skgrepo at 'fred/public', and only 'me/'
  exists, with two empty folders. Its README says to look for "'lens',
  'subscribe', 'override' or (soon) 'fork'": 'lens' appears in 'docs/'
  only as the name of an engine inside the clients, and forks are built.
  Change: ship a 'fred/public' of three or four notes about something
  ordinary, which would also give the reader someone else's notes to
  view on the first day; and reword the README to "subscribe",
  "override" and "fork".
